section: teardown
title: Teardown and leftovers
about: |
  What a run before can leave in the cloud and in Palette, and what a force delete leaves behind.
  The lab checks these with its inventory scripts before a build; a company checks its own estate.
rules:
- id: name-prefix
  title: No pool name is a prefix of another
  engines:
  - all
  - lab
  tier: static
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  what: |
    The lab inventory finds resources by a name prefix (`name ~ ^<name>`), so `fred` matches
    `fred-b` as well, and a count or a delete of one cluster touches the other. The row is about
    cluster names, and one entity names one cluster. The check applies the same rule to the pool
    names of the entity: a pool name that starts another pool name is refused. Choose names that
    share no prefix.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | .poolConfig.name // "" ] as $names
      | [ $names[] as $a | $names[] as $b
          | select($a != "" and $a != $b and ($b | startswith($a)))
          | "pool \($a) is a prefix of pool \($b); a prefix search matches both" ]
      | unique
  fix:
    owner: lab
    text: Match names exactly, or give each cluster and pool a name that is no prefix of another.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    ref: examples/live/gcp-inventory.sh
    note: the filter `name ~ ^$name` matches every name with the prefix
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/aws/pool-name-prefix.json
    clean: fixtures/aws/clean.json
- id: versions-outside-state
  title: Palette holds no version outside the state
  engines:
  - all
  tier: palette
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  what: |
    With `skip_destroy`, a bump keeps the replaced version in Palette and drops it from the
    OpenTofu state. A destroy then removes the current version alone; the older versions of the
    name stay. The world has no state to compare with, so strata-preflight lists nothing here.
    List the versions by name, and delete each one the state does not hold.
  reproduce:
  - 'strata list profiles --json | jq -r --arg n {{ .profiles[0].source.name // "<profile name>" }} ''.profiles[] | select(.name == $n) | .version''   # every version of the name in Palette'
  - 'tofu state list | grep spectrocloud_cluster_profile   # the versions the state holds'
  - 'examples/live/api.sh delete-named {{ .profiles[0].source.name // "<profile name>" }}   # the fix of the lab: every version of the name'
  fix:
    owner: lab
    text: Delete by name after the destroy; `just live-down` runs `api.sh delete-named`.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    ref: examples/live/api.sh delete-named
    note: deletes the versions that skip_destroy kept out of the OpenTofu state
  - kind: source
    ref: docs/src/development/live-example.md
    note: skip_destroy keeps the versions that a bump replaced out of the state
- id: macro-undeletable
  title: No cluster reads a macro before its delete
  engines:
  - all
  tier: palette
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  what: |
    Palette refuses to delete a project macro that a cluster reads. A teardown that deletes the
    macro before the cluster fails at that step. The values and the manifests of the packs name
    each macro they read as a `.spectro.macro.NAME` template, and `strata snapshot --macros`
    records them for a cluster. The world has no project uid, so strata-preflight cannot call
    `GET /v1/projects/{uid}/macros` here; the lab calls it through `api.sh`.
  reproduce:
  - 'examples/live/api.sh get /v1/projects/$PALETTE_PROJECT_UID/macros | jq -r ''.macros[].name''   # the macros of the project'
  - 'strata snapshot cluster:{{ .clusterUid // "<cluster uid>" }} --macros --json | jq ''.macros''   # the macros the cluster reads'
  fix:
    owner: none
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: macro-repave lab
    note: Palette also refuses to delete a macro that a cluster reads (docs/src/internals/palette/profiles.md)
